/*  Matrices — `a matrix with ((1, 2), (3, 4))`, `a matrix with 2 by 3 filled with 0`,
    `item at (r, c) of m`, `The item at (r, c) of m becomes v.`, `the rows of m`, `the columns of m`,
    and the arithmetic: `m * 2` and `2 * m`, and `+`, `-` and `*` between two matrices.

    ★ A matrix is the runtime's own `CufetMatrix*`, numbers row by row in the arena, counted from 1
      and bounds-checked by the runtime with the interpreter's messages.

    ★ Scaling cannot fail — there are no sizes to disagree — so it gives a matrix. Two matrices
      added, taken away or multiplied CAN fail, when their sizes do not fit: that gives
      `failure of matrix`, read as its value inside a `Try` as a call that can fail is.
*/

Pull books on collections, and the c-language.
    /// Whether a binary expression is matrix arithmetic: a matrix on either side of `+`, `-` or `*`.
    Bind fact or failure to is-matrix-binary unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define operator as (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s word.
        If operator is not "Plus" and operator is not "Minus" and operator is not "Star", return false.
        Define left-kind as cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Define right-kind as cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)) or pass the failure off.
        Return left-kind is "matrix" or right-kind is "matrix".
    Done.

    /// What matrix arithmetic gives, as it reads here: scaling a matrix, the sum, difference or
    /// product of two — which may fail.
    Bind text or failure to matrix-binary-kind unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define left-kind as cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Define right-kind as cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)) or pass the failure off.
        If left-kind is "matrix" and right-kind is "matrix":
            Cast one's register-failable on ("failure of matrix").
            Return cast one's unwrapped-kind on ("failure of matrix").
        Done.
        Return "matrix".
    Done.

    /// Matrix arithmetic as C, its two sides worked out in the order written.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-matrix-binary unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define left-side as cast field-of on (expression, 1).
        Define right-side as cast field-of on (expression, 3).
        Define left-kind as cast one's kind-of on (left-side) or pass the failure off.
        Define right-kind as cast one's kind-of on (right-side) or pass the failure off.
        Define left-c as cast one's c-of on (left-side) or pass the failure off.
        Define right-c as cast one's c-of on (right-side) or pass the failure off.
        Define sides as a series of c-language axiom with (left-c, right-c).
        Define prefix as cast order-prefix on (a series of node with (left-side, right-side), sides).
        If left-kind is not "matrix", return cast in-order on (prefix, call-of-two on ("cufet_mat_scale", item 2 of sides, item 1 of sides)).
        If right-kind is not "matrix", return cast in-order on (prefix, call-of-two on ("cufet_mat_scale", item 1 of sides, item 2 of sides)).
        Define operator as (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s word.
        Define called as "cufet_mat_mul".
        Define said as "left matrix columns must equal right matrix rows for matrix product".
        If operator is "Plus":
            The called becomes "cufet_mat_add".
            The said becomes "matrices must have equal dimensions for addition".
        Done.
        Otherwise if operator is "Minus":
            The called becomes "cufet_mat_sub".
            The said becomes "matrices must have equal dimensions for subtraction".
        Done.
        Cast one's register-failable on ("failure of matrix").
        Define type-c as cast failable-c-name on ("failure of matrix").
        Define c-language matrix-worked, given (the term called, the c-language axiom left, the c-language axiom right, the term some, the term fail, the text said),
            as [({ CufetMatrix* cf_mr = the called(the left, the right); cf_mr ? the some(cf_mr) : the fail((CufetFailure){ the said, "dimension-mismatch" }); })].
        Define worked as matrix-worked on (called, item 1 of sides, item 2 of sides, "{type-c}_some", "{type-c}_fail", said).
        Return cast one's c-unwrapped on (cast in-order on (prefix, worked), "failure of matrix").
    Done.

    /// The kind of a matrix expression: a matrix, or the number an item is.
    Bind text to matrix-kind-of, given (the node expression):
        If expression's kind is "MatrixAccess", return "number".
        Return "matrix".
    Done.

    /// A matrix expression as C.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-matrix-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as expression's kind.
        If kind is "MatrixLiteral":
            // Its rows as written, each element worked out in order, row by row.
            Define rows as (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s children.
            Define width as the number of (item 1 of rows)'s children.
            Define c-language element-set, given (the c-language axiom built, the number place, the c-language axiom element),
                as [the built cf_mt->data[the place] = the element;].
            Define built as cast no-c.
            Define place as 0.
            For each row in rows, repeat:
                For each element in row's children, repeat:
                    Define element-c as cast one's c-of-as on (element, "number") or pass the failure off.
                    The built becomes element-set on (built, place, element-c).
                    Increment place by 1.
                Done.
            Done.
            Define c-language matrix-made, given (the number height, the number width, the c-language axiom built),
                as [({ CufetMatrix* cf_mt = cufet_mat_new(the height, the width); the built cf_mt; })].
            Return matrix-made on (the number of rows, width, built).
        Done.
        Define at-line as cast line-number on (cast field-of on (expression, 4)).
        If kind is "MatrixSized":
            Define operands as a series of node with (cast field-of on (expression, 1), cast field-of on (expression, 2)).
            Define emitted as a series of c-language axiom.
            Define rows-c as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (expression, 1), "number") or pass the failure off.
            Insert rows-c into emitted.
            Define columns-c as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (expression, 2), "number") or pass the failure off.
            Insert columns-c into emitted.
            Define filled as call-of-one on ("cufet_dec_from_ll", [0]).
            If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)) is false:
                Insert cast field-of on (expression, 3) into operands.
                Define fill-c as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (expression, 3), "number") or pass the failure off.
                Insert fill-c into emitted.
            Done.
            Define prefix as cast order-prefix on (operands, emitted).
            If the number of emitted is 3, the filled becomes item 3 of emitted.
            Define c-language matrix-sized, given (the c-language axiom height, the c-language axiom width, the c-language axiom filled, the number at-line),
                as [cufet_mat_sized(the height, the width, the filled, the at-line)].
            Return cast in-order on (prefix, matrix-sized on (item 1 of emitted, item 2 of emitted, filled, at-line)).
        Done.
        // `item at (r, c) of m` — the matrix, then the row, then the column.
        Define operands as a series of node with (cast field-of on (expression, 1), cast field-of on (expression, 2), cast field-of on (expression, 3)).
        Define emitted as a series of c-language axiom.
        Define matrix-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Insert matrix-c into emitted.
        Define row-c as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (expression, 2), "number") or pass the failure off.
        Insert row-c into emitted.
        Define column-c as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (expression, 3), "number") or pass the failure off.
        Insert column-c into emitted.
        Define prefix as cast order-prefix on (operands, emitted).
        Define c-language matrix-item, given (the c-language axiom grid, the c-language axiom row, the c-language axiom column, the number at-line),
            as [cufet_mat_get(the grid, cufet_to_int(the row), cufet_to_int(the column), the at-line)].
        Return cast in-order on (prefix, matrix-item on (item 1 of emitted, item 2 of emitted, item 3 of emitted, at-line)).
    Done.

    /// `The item at (r, c) of m becomes v.` — the matrix, the row, the column, then the value.
    Bind void or failure to emit-matrix-set unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        Define operands as a series of node with (cast field-of on (statement, 1), cast field-of on (statement, 2), cast field-of on (statement, 3), cast field-of on (statement, 4)).
        Define emitted as a series of c-language axiom.
        Define matrix-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Insert matrix-c into emitted.
        Define row-c as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (statement, 2), "number") or pass the failure off.
        Insert row-c into emitted.
        Define column-c as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (statement, 3), "number") or pass the failure off.
        Insert column-c into emitted.
        Define value-c as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (statement, 4), "number") or pass the failure off.
        Insert value-c into emitted.
        Define prefix as cast order-prefix on (operands, emitted).
        Define c-language item-stored, given (the c-language axiom grid, the c-language axiom row, the c-language axiom column, the c-language axiom value, the number at-line),
            as [cufet_mat_set(the grid, cufet_to_int(the row), cufet_to_int(the column), the value, the at-line);].
        Define stored as item-stored on (item 1 of emitted, item 2 of emitted, item 3 of emitted, item 4 of emitted, cast line-number on (cast field-of on (statement, 5))).
        Cast one's put on (cast in-order-statement on (prefix, stored)).
    Done.

    /// `the rows of m`, `the columns of m` as C.
    Bind c-language axiom to c-matrix-count, given (the c-language axiom matrix-c, the text field-name):
        Define c-language rows-held, given (the c-language axiom grid), as [cufet_dec_from_ll((the grid)->rows)].
        Define c-language columns-held, given (the c-language axiom grid), as [cufet_dec_from_ll((the grid)->cols)].
        If field-name is "rows", return rows-held on (matrix-c).
        Return columns-held on (matrix-c).
    Done.
Done.
